<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <PackageId>Talaan</PackageId>
    <Version>0.4.0</Version>
    <Authors>BaryoDev</Authors>
    <Description>A zero-dependency spreadsheet and CSV reader and writer for .NET. Reads and writes .xlsx (OOXML) and CSV into a simple typed cell grid, no Interop, no ClosedXML, no OpenXML SDK.</Description>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MPL-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageTags>xlsx;csv;tsv;spreadsheet;excel;parser;writer;zero-dependency;import;export</PackageTags>

    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/BaryoDev/Talaan</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/BaryoDev/Talaan</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>

    <PackageReleaseNotes>0.4.0
- New: XlsxReadOptions.MaxCells is an opt-in cap on cells per worksheet. A sheet that would hold more throws InvalidDataException. There is no limit by default.
- CSV: a quote in the middle of an unquoted field opens quoted mode, so it can merge rows or throw. Unchanged, now documented. Quote any field that contains a quote.
- Dates: in the 1900 date system, serials 1 to 59 read one day earlier than Excel shows. Unchanged, now documented.
- Correction: the 0.3.0 note below listed CsvWriter.Write(Stream, IEnumerable&lt;SheetData&gt;). That overload does not exist. CsvWriter only has Write(Stream, SheetData, char delimiter).
- Reading an .xlsx part nested deeper than 256 levels, a non-numeric numFmtId, or a relationship target that climbs above the package root throws InvalidDataException.
- Relationship targets such as ../xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml now resolve.
- Cell values are read as invariant numbers: "1,5" is no longer read as 15, and NaN and infinity stay text.

0.3.0
New:
- Spreadsheet.WriteXlsx(Stream, IEnumerable&lt;SheetData&gt;) writes every sheet to an .xlsx and leaves the stream open.
- Spreadsheet.WriteFile(path, sheets) picks the format from the extension (.xlsx every sheet, .csv and .tsv the first sheet), writes a temp file and moves it into place.
- CsvWriter.Write(Stream, SheetData, char delimiter) and CsvWriter.Write(Stream, IEnumerable&lt;SheetData&gt;) write RFC 4180 CSV or TSV as UTF-8 without a BOM.

Writing rules:
- Text is written as inline strings, so "00123" stays text. Numbers use invariant culture and round-trip. NaN and infinity throw.
- Dates are serial numbers formatted yyyy-mm-dd, or yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss when they have a time, and read back as dates. Dates before 1900-03-01 throw.
- Invalid sheet names, an empty sheet list and cell text over 32767 characters throw ArgumentException, and nothing is written.
- Characters XML 1.0 forbids are dropped from text and sheet names.
- No styling, formulas, column widths or merged cells.</PackageReleaseNotes>

    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>

    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\assets\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
